      "text": "Price action reflects conflicting signals at the analysis cutoff. The November 3 close of $483.90 was below the 50-day average of $548.70 but above the 200-day average of $412.94; RSI14 was 38.41 and MACD histogram was -9.48. On November 4 the quote snapshot was $484.52, while the regular session was still in progress when captured, so completed-session indicators remain anchored to November 3. <<metric:market-session.close|period>> <<metric:market-session.sma50|period>> <<metric:market-session.sma200|period>> <<metric:market-session.rsi14|period>> <<metric:market-session.macdHistogram|period>>",
      "sourceIds": ["verified-snapshot-AMD", "market-yahoo-equity-amd"]
    },
    {
      "text": "Near-term operating catalysts include the Q4 2026 report and follow-through on the earnings release’s stated plan to scale Helios and Venice production. The upcoming earnings date of February 1, 2027 is provider-estimated and not issuer-confirmed. Reported demand, production scale, and margins will clarify whether current growth converts into sustained profitable shipments.",
