    },
    {
      "text": "The price-action discussion should remain descriptive. The November 3 close was below the 50-day average but above the 200-day average, while RSI14 and MACD histogram reflected recent weakness; those mixed indicators do not independently corroborate either the operating thesis or a directional market outcome. The November 4 quote was captured during an unfinished session and should not be treated as a closing response to earnings. <<metric:market-session.close|period>> <<metric:market-session.sma50|period>> <<metric:market-session.sma200|period>> <<metric:market-session.rsi14|period>> <<metric:market-session.macdHistogram|period>>",
      "sourceIds": ["verified-snapshot-AMD", "market-yahoo-equity-amd"]
    },
    {
      "text": "The scenarios are useful as conditional operating paths, but the evidence does not rank them. The bull path relies on Helios and Venice scaling; the middle path relies on supply or deployment constraints; the bear path relies on competition, cyclicality, or execution problems. The supplied release contains management’s expectation of accelerating Q4 growth and its production plan, while the filing identifies relevant risks; neither source quantifies scenario likelihood or deployment scale. Keep these as alternatives rather than implying a probability-weighted outlook.",
      "sourceIds": ["extended-sec-edgar-amd-8k-0000002488-26-000188", "extended-sec-edgar-amd-10q", "extended-sec-edgar-amd-10k"]
    },
    {
      "text": "Historical misses argue for caution specifically on short-horizon price inference: the October 28 outside-range call resolved inside its range, and the October 26 five-session relative-performance call missed as AMD underperformed SPY. These outcomes do not refute the operating thesis, but they do weaken any attempt to infer near-term direction from a sharp move or earnings reaction alone.",
      "sourceIds": ["history-report-2026-10-28T15-00-19-942Z-3187f78d", "history-report-2026-10-26T15-45-16-421Z-0600df32"]
    }
